WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.256 --> 00:00:05.783
- This isn't the chapter I studied for!

00:00:06.621 --> 00:00:09.261
(sobbing)

00:00:10.078 --> 00:00:11.454
(thud)

00:00:11.454 --> 00:00:13.264
I could have ruined my life.

00:00:13.264 --> 00:00:14.972
I'm gonna be a meth head on the street.

00:00:14.972 --> 00:00:16.625
(thuds against plastic)

00:00:16.625 --> 00:00:18.321
You're tricking me to
thinking that it's "this",

00:00:18.321 --> 00:00:20.486
but really, really it's "that".

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:21.470
(thud against plastic)

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:24.599
The last 10 I've done 'C' so

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:26.630
there is no other answer but 'C'.

00:00:26.630 --> 00:00:28.763
If I spell my name right, does that count?

00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:30.528
I heard that counts.

00:00:30.528 --> 00:00:33.981
Skip it, skip it, skip it, skip it.

00:00:33.981 --> 00:00:35.610
Skip it, skip it.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.793
I'm gonna have the best
time on New Year's Eve

00:00:37.793 --> 00:00:39.369
and kiss a boy.

00:00:39.369 --> 00:00:42.235
(heavy metal music)

00:00:42.235 --> 00:00:44.326
Plenty of rich people
dropped out of college.

00:00:44.326 --> 00:00:45.957
I'm gonna be rich!

00:00:45.957 --> 00:00:50.726
Siri, what's the answer to question 42.

00:00:50.726 --> 00:00:52.453
- [Voiceover] Okay, I
found this on the Web

00:00:52.453 --> 00:00:54.627
for "what's the answer
to question 42 feet".

00:00:54.627 --> 00:00:55.770
- No!

00:00:55.770 --> 00:00:58.640
E quals mc squared times the number

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:00.661
of Meryl Streep's Oscars to the pair of X

00:01:00.661 --> 00:01:03.038
divided by the number of snubs she has got

00:01:03.038 --> 00:01:04.246
and minus the hours of sleep

00:01:04.246 --> 00:01:05.536
that I personally have lost.

00:01:05.536 --> 00:01:09.418
That equals 93 billion light years

00:01:09.418 --> 00:01:13.580
which is approximately the size
of the observable Universe.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:16.767
So, in comparison

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:19.474
why does any of this matter?

00:01:19.474 --> 00:01:21.008
Shall I go back to that
question I skipped?

00:01:21.008 --> 00:01:22.665
Forget it!

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:25.286
We're all just star dust anyway.

00:01:25.286 --> 00:01:30.282
(techno music)

00:01:30.952 --> 00:01:33.087
- [Voiceover] All right, exam is over.

00:01:33.087 --> 00:01:35.261
Hand in your sheets.

00:01:35.261 --> 00:01:39.958
(paper rustling)

00:01:41.498 --> 00:01:42.718
- Yeah,

00:01:42.718 --> 00:01:44.110
that went well.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:44.945
Yeah.

